@user:A{nm=~13:Project owner;rl=user}
@v_aid_faithful:V{at=~10:2026-09-14;ev=[@e_aid_faithful];rq=@q_aid_faithful;st=pass;tk=@t_aid;wh=@actor;wy=~278:All 36 panels were checked block by block: 14,040 opaque source pixels each enlarge into a uniform z-by-z block of the identical colour, with zero non-uniform blocks and zero colours absent from the source files. This is enlargement fidelity only and carries no artistic weight.;xr=@x_aid}
@v_aid_useful:V{at=~10:2026-09-14;ev=[@e_aid_useful];rq=@q_aid_useful;st=pass;tk=@t_aid;wh=@actor;wy=~411:The sheet was viewed in this session. It shows both treatments at all six sampled scales over light, dark and busy backgrounds, and it surfaced a finding neither reference shows alone: the navy outline loses the figure against dark backgrounds but is what separates it against busy ones. Stated limit: at 1x the two treatments are not reliably distinguishable, so the sheet supports the decision from 3x upward.;xr=@x_aid}
@v_study_complete:V{at=~10:2026-09-14;ev=[@e_study_complete];rq=@q_study_complete;st=pass;tk=@t_study;wh=@actor;wy=~313:Every declared completeness check passed when run against the retained study: both reference hashes, the exact 180-pixel difference and its single colour-substitution nature, and the unresolved projection, role, scale and animation questions are all stated. This is a textual check and carries no artistic weight.;xr=@x_study}
@v_study_seen:V{at=~10:2026-09-14;ev=[@e_study_seen];rq=@q_study_seen;st=pass;tk=@t_study;wh=@actor;wy=~417:Both references were opened at native 32x32 and at 12x nearest-neighbour enlargement in this session. At native scale the outline difference was not reliably judgeable; the enlargement is what made it legible. What was seen matches the study, including that the navy in reference.png also carries the shoulder bar, base bar and solid stalks, so the unoutlined variant loses those landmarks and not merely the contour.;xr=@x_study}
@x_aid:X{dg=~64:eacc9b6633ddf4e02d07caa24565512c08f0a659ca07e53fb456c20748856270;kd=reference;nm=~42:Outline and display-scale comparison sheet;of=@f_aid;ur=~41:deliverables/outline-scale-comparison.png}
@x_study:X{dg=~64:d0862d144da0c4b315af96a8129846b32075fac99826b618ad51c62b6a960495;kd=report;nm=~48:Reference measurement and outline-conflict study;of=@f_study;ur=~33:sources/reference-observations.md}
